            Joke("When I spoke of wise things, no one came. So I whistled.", "A crowd came running. Men run to nonsense, and stroll to wisdom."),
            Joke("Scholars study the troubles of Odysseus, not their own.", "Yours are easy to study. There is just one, and you push it every day."),
            Joke("Men tune the lyre, and leave their souls out of tune.", "You have one string and one song: push. It is never out of tune."),
            Joke("Some men study the moon, and miss what lies at their feet.", "You never miss what is at your feet. It is big, grey and round."),
            Joke("Hold out your hand to a friend with the fingers open.", "A fist gives nothing. And an open hand pushes a rock better. You know."),
            Joke("Pirates sold me in Crete. The crier asked what I could do.", "I said: Rule men. Sell me to that man in purple. He needs a master."),
            Joke("At the slave market, they told me not to sit down.", "I said: Fish lie any way they like, and still they find buyers."),
            Joke("When men buy a pot, they tap it to hear if it rings true.", "When they choose a man, they only look. I have listened to you. You ring true."),
            Joke("I taught my master's sons to serve themselves.", "To eat plain food, drink water and go barefoot. You would be my best pupil."),
            Joke("My master asked how I wished to be buried. I said: Face down.", "Soon, down will turn into up. You know how that goes."),
            Joke("Alexander said: If I were not Alexander, I would be Diogenes.", "And if I were not Diogenes? I would be Diogenes. I like my jar."),
            Joke("Men praise me as a fine hunting dog.", "But none will come hunting with me. Too far, too hard. You would come."),
            Joke("They told me: You are old, Diogenes. Take a rest.", "Does a runner slow down near the finish? No, he runs faster. So do you."),
            Joke("I was asked to dinner, and I said no.", "The last time I went, my host did not thank me enough."),
            Joke("A man dropped his bread, and was too ashamed to pick it up.", "So I dragged a jar on a rope across the market. A load is no shame."),
            Joke("When I gave my master orders, he cried: Rivers run uphill!", "Rivers never run uphill, I said. Rocks do, with a little help."),
            Joke("A man asked to be my pupil. I gave him a cheese to carry.", "He would not carry it. A cheese worth half an obol broke our friendship."),
            Joke("The gods own all things. The wise are friends of the gods.", "And friends share all. So your rock is mine. Do keep pushing it for me."),
            Joke("All the curses of the old plays fell on me.", "No home, no city, I beg for my bread. But no god gave me a rock. Lucky me."),
            Joke("A man read for hours. At last, we saw the end of his scroll.", "I cried: Cheer up, men! Land in sight! I say the same to you, near the top."),
            Joke("A man proved to me, with logic, that I have horns.", "I touched my forehead and said: Well, I do not see any."),
