            Joke("As I left the baths, a man asked: Are there many men inside?", "I said: No. Then another asked: Is it crowded? I said: Yes, very."),
            Joke("Men pray for what seems good to them, not for what is good.", "You never pray for a lighter rock. A wise man, or a tired one."),
            Joke("Men care so much about what they do in their dreams.", "And so little about what they do awake. You, at least, push wide awake."),
            Joke("A boy broke my jar. The people of Athens gave me a new one.", "That is how I knew they loved me. Nobody gives a jar to a man he hates."),
            Joke("After the battle, King Philip asked me who I was.", "I said: A spy on your greed. He liked that, and he let me go."),
            Joke("The gods gave men an easy life.", "We buried it under honey cakes and sweet oils. Yours is under a rock."),
            Joke("Some boys cried: Watch out, the Dog will bite us!", "I said: Do not fear, boys. A dog does not eat beetroot."),
            Joke("A man wore a lion skin, as Heracles did.", "I said: Do not shame the coat of courage. Earn it first, with a labor or two."),
            Joke("Men call Callisthenes lucky: he eats with Alexander.", "Unlucky, I said. He may eat only when Alexander says so."),
            Joke("When I need money, I do not beg my friends for gifts.", "I ask them to pay back what they owe me. I gave them a lot of wisdom."),
            Joke("Riddle: a sheep with a golden fleece, on two legs. What is it?", "A rich man who knows nothing. Fine to look at. Do not ask him the way."),
            Joke("I once went to a very dirty bathhouse.", "I asked: After people wash in it, where do they go to get clean?"),
            Joke("One singer always lost his crowd. I called him: Rooster!", "Why? Because when he sings, everyone gets up."),
