            Joke("They mock me for being sent away from my city.", "But that is how I became a wise man. And a rock is how you became strong."),
            Joke("The people of Sinope sent me away forever.", "So I sentenced them to stay at home forever. Fair is fair."),
            Joke("When I ask for money, I always say the same thing.", "If you gave to someone else, give to me too. If you did not, start with me."),
            Joke("How does Dionysius the tyrant treat his friends?", "Like purses. Full, he hangs them up. Empty, he throws them away."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is the mother of all evils?", "The love of money. So I keep my money in other men's purses."),
            Joke("Riddle: which animal has the worst bite?", "Of the wild ones, the slanderer. Of the tame ones, the flatterer."),
            Joke("Sweet words are honey that sticks in your throat.", "So no sweet words from me. Your rock is heavy, and you are stubborn. There."),
            Joke("Riddle: why is gold so pale?", "Fear. So many thieves are after it. Your rock has a healthy grey."),
            Joke("Good men are the images of the gods.", "Hold still, Sisyphus. Let me look at you. No, push on. It suits you better."),
            Joke("I have no servant. They asked me: Who will bury you, then?", "I said: Whoever wants my house. It is a jar, so it may take a while."),
            Joke("Plato talks of tablehood and cuphood.", "I said: Table and cup, I can see. Tablehood and cuphood, I cannot."),
            Joke("Someone asked Plato: What sort of man is Diogenes?", "He said: A Socrates gone mad. I took it as praise. Half of it, anyway."),
            Joke("A man asked what I would take to let him box my ears.", "I said: A helmet."),
            Joke("I saw a young man blush, and I said: Courage!", "That is the color of goodness. Your face is red too. Is it the climb?"),
            Joke("Two men went to law, and I judged against them both.", "One had surely stolen. The other had surely lost nothing."),
            Joke("They told me: Many people laugh at you.", "I said: But I am not laughed down. Your rock rolls down. You never do."),
            Joke("A man told me that life is a bad thing.", "I said: Not life. Living badly. You live uphill, but you live well."),
            Joke("My servant Manes ran away. My friends said: Go after him!", "I said: If Manes can live without me, I can live without Manes."),
            Joke("Someone hid a cake among my olives. I threw it out.", "I said: Stranger, make way for the princes! The olives, I mean."),
            Joke("Do wise men eat cakes?", "Yes. All kinds of cakes, just like other men. Do you have one? No? Pity."),
            Joke("Why do men give to beggars, and not to wise men?", "They fear they may be lame or blind one day. Never that they will be wise."),
            Joke("A man mocked me: You made false coins once!", "I said: Then I was what you are now. What I am now, you will never be."),
            Joke("I came to a tiny town with very big gates.", "I said: Shut your gates, or your town will run away through them."),
            Joke("A teacher spoke on and on. So I held up a salted fish.", "His pupils came to look. One obol of fish broke up his whole class."),
            Joke("They scold me for eating in the market.", "But the market is where I got hungry. Where do you eat? Halfway up, I bet."),
            Joke("Plato said: Serve the king, and you need not wash lettuce.", "I said: Wash lettuce, and you need not serve the king."),
