            Joke("I owned a goat once.", "By the end of the week, the goat owned me. Things are like that."),
            Joke("People ask how I got so old.", "No things, no fuss, and a nap after lunch. And one before lunch."),
            Joke("A rich man asked me the way to be happy.", "I said: Put down the gold, and walk. He put down a little, and walked a little."),
            Joke("A king has a palace and a thousand guards.", "I have a jar, and no guards at all. Guess which of us sleeps better."),
            Joke("Rich men spend half their lives counting their gold.", "You have one rock. You never lose count. That is a kind of freedom."),
            Joke("Gold can buy anything, people say.", "Then let it buy my friend a flat hill. We will wait."),
            Joke("Fame is like your rock.", "Hard to push up, and it comes down by itself. I leave mine at the bottom."),
            Joke("You were a king once, with gold and a palace.", "Now you have a rock and a hill. A good trade, I think. Fewer things to dust."),
            Joke("You and I both live outside, and both work for nothing.", "We should start a school. No. Then people would come."),
            Joke("Be careful what you say in front of writers.", "I said a few odd things. Now they are in books, and much funnier."),
            Joke("They say Plutus, the god of wealth, is blind.", "So he gives gold to anyone he bumps into. I keep well out of his way."),
            Joke("A traveler asked me for the quickest way to the top.", "I said: Follow the man with the rock. It is not quick, but he knows it best."),
            Joke("Do I care what people think? Of course I do.", "I think about them all the time. That is why I live in a jar."),
            Joke("Zeus has thunder. Hades rules the dead.", "And the best they could think of for you was a rock? I expected more of gods."),
            Joke("The gods have everything, and they are always cross.", "I have nothing, and I am in a fine mood. Think about it on the way up."),
            Joke("The hill is steep, the rock is heavy, the top is far.", "Still, nobody makes you dress for dinner. Count your blessings."),
            Joke("Some say the rock is your fate.", "I say it is your rock. Fate is a big word for a stone."),
            Joke("Protagoras says man is the measure of all things.", "So your rock weighs exactly one Sisyphus. I always thought so."),
            Joke("Plato says men sit in a cave and look at shadows.", "And they call me odd. At least I come out of my jar in the morning."),
            Joke("Socrates said: All I know is that I know nothing.", "I know that too. I just say it in fewer words."),
            Joke("Aristotle teaches as he walks, and his pupils follow.", "You walk too. Your pupil is a rock. It runs off at the end of every lesson."),
            Joke("Aristotle says the best is always in the middle.", "So you are at your best halfway up. Rest there. Tell him I said so."),
            Joke("Anaxagoras says the sun is only a hot stone.", "So someone rolls a hot stone across the sky each day. Yours, at least, is cool."),
            Joke("Heraclitus says you never step in the same river twice.", "But the same rock, you push every day. Rocks are more loyal than rivers."),
            Joke("Heraclitus says the way up and the way down are one.", "He never pushed a rock. The way down is much faster."),
            Joke("Parmenides says that nothing ever really changes.", "I think he watched you for a day, and then wrote it down."),
            Joke("Democritus says all things are made of tiny bits.", "Your rock too. Ten thousand tiny bits, and every one wants to go down."),
            Joke("Pythagoras says souls come back in new bodies.", "Next time, I want to be a dog. They tell me I am halfway there."),
            Joke("Pythagoras says the stars make music as they turn.", "Your rock makes music too, on the way down. Mostly drums."),
            Joke("Delphi says: Know yourself.", "I did. It took one morning. There is not much to me."),
            Joke("Delphi says: Nothing in excess.", "I agree. I have nothing, and I am careful never to have too much of it."),
            Joke("The philosophers talk all day about the good life.", "You and I just live it. Well, I live it. You push it."),
            Joke("You are the most patient man I know.", "And I once sat through a whole lecture by Plato."),
            Joke("I would help you push, but I am a philosopher.", "We are very good at explaining why a rock is heavy."),
            Joke("Your days are all the same, they say.", "So are mine, and I chose it. You got yours for free. Lucky man."),
            Joke("If you ever reach the top and the rock stays, call me.", "I will bring my lamp. That, I want to see."),
            Joke("They say you were the cleverest man alive. You tricked Death.", "That is how it goes with clever men. They always end up pushing something."),
            Joke("I have watched you for a while now.", "You never complain. I complain for a living. I am worried for my job."),
            Joke("You push all day, and never say a word.", "I talk all day, and push nothing. Together we would make one wise man."),
            Joke("Every day you push, and every day I watch.", "I think I have the better job. But you have the better legs."),
            Joke("You know what I like about your rock?", "It has never once tried to be a bigger rock. Most men cannot say that."),
            Joke("Some men push gold. Some men push their luck.", "Yours is a rock. I like a man who knows what he is pushing."),
            Joke("Do you ever wish your rock were smaller?", "Careful. Then a smaller hill, then a smaller life. Then one day, a jar."),
            Joke("People ask why you push the same rock every day.", "I ask why they carry the same worries every day. You at least get a view."),
            Joke("The gods meant your rock to make you suffer.", "No master, no debts, no taxes, and nobody to argue with. Gods are bad at this."),
            Joke("The top must be a fine place.", "You never stay long enough to tell me about it."),
            Joke("What is at the top, I wonder?", "If it is nothing, then I live there already. Come and visit."),
            Joke("When your rock rolls down, thank it.", "It saved you carrying it down. Very kind, for a rock."),
            Joke("At the top, when it gets away from you, do you shout?", "I would. Something short and wise, like: Oh well. Then I would go and get it."),
            Joke("I do not envy you the rock. I envy you the hill.", "The wind, the view, and no philosophers. Well, one."),
            Joke("You will push forever, I hear. Forever is a long time.", "Push slowly, then. It makes no difference, and it looks wise."),
            Joke("I tried to push a rock once.", "It wanted to go down. I let it. We parted as friends."),
            Joke("Poor Tantalus wants fruit he can never reach.", "I want nothing, so I always get it. Someone should tell him the trick."),
            Joke("Your rock is your oldest friend, and the hill your oldest enemy.", "I am your newest friend. Hello. I promise not to roll away."),
            Joke("You are the only man I know who knows where he is going.", "Up. Always up. And then, for a short while, down."),
            Joke("Riddle: what goes all around the tree, but never goes in?", "The bark. I am the Dog, so bark is my trade."),
            Joke("Riddle: when is a door not a door?", "When it is ajar. A jar is my door, my house and my bed."),
            Joke("Riddle: the poor have it, and the rich need it.", "Nothing. I have more of it than anyone. I am the richest man alive."),
            Joke("Riddle: what has many teeth, but never bites?", "A comb. I have never owned one. Look at my beard. You can tell."),
            Joke("Riddle: what goes into a jar at night, and comes out wiser?", "Me. Well, older. Wiser takes longer."),
            Joke("Riddle: what gets wetter, the more it dries?", "A towel. I have none. When I get wet, I shake, like a dog. Much cheaper."),
            Joke("Riddle: who has truer friends, a king or a beggar?", "The beggar. Nobody makes friends with him for his gold."),
            Joke("Riddle: it fills a room, but takes up no room at all.", "Light. My jar is small, so my lamp fills it very fast."),
            Joke("Riddle: the same weight all day, and heavier by evening.", "Your rock. The rock never changes. The evening does."),
            Joke("Riddle: no house, no money, no shoes, and no worries.", "Me. Or the Dog. Call either name, and I come running."),
            Joke("Riddle: thrown out when it is needed, taken in when it is not.", "An anchor. Throw your rock into the sea one day. Then it is the sea's problem."),
            Joke("Riddle: which is older, your rock or your hill?", "The hill, by far. But the rock has seen much more of it."),
            Joke("Riddle: who has heard all my jokes, and never laughed once?", "Your rock. It may be the wisest of us all."),
            Joke("Riddle: four legs at dawn, two at noon, three at dusk.", "Man, says the Sphinx. Some days I go on four. They call me the Dog for a reason."),
            Joke("Riddle: the more you have, the more it weighs on you.", "Things. I have none, so I am light as a bird. You have one, and look at it."),
            Joke("Riddle: the higher you push it, the harder it falls.", "Your rock. Also pride. Push the rock, and leave the pride at the bottom."),
            Joke("Riddle: men chase it all their lives, and it never stays.", "A coin. You chase a rock. It never stays either, but it is much easier to find."),
            Joke("Riddle: what carries its house on its back, everywhere?", "A snail. I thought of carrying my jar like that. Then I saw you. No, thank you."),
            Joke("Riddle: who works all day, earns nothing, and spends nothing?", "You. I earn nothing and spend nothing too, but I skip the work."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is the shortest book of philosophy?", "Mine. One page: Want less. You could read it on the way up."),
            Joke("Riddle: what do Plato and your rock have in common?", "Both are heavy, and with both, you end up back where you began."),
            Joke("Riddle: who is the one man who never needs a map?", "You. Up, then down, then up again. Even I could not get lost."),
            Joke("Riddle: it has no legs, but it wins every race down the hill.", "Your rock. You come second, every time. Do not feel bad."),
            Joke("Riddle: what does a dog chase all day, and never catch?", "His tail. You chase the top. You catch it, and your rock runs off."),
            Joke("Riddle: one goes up slowly, the other comes down fast.", "You and your rock. You are the slow one. Do not tell it I said so."),
            Joke("Riddle: what do I need to light a lamp at noon?", "A lamp, some oil, and no shame at all. The last is the easy part."),
            Joke("Riddle: you take it for a walk every day, but it never walks.", "Your rock. Like a lazy dog. And it will not fetch itself. You have to."),
        ),
    ),
    Joker(
        1, "Alice", 124,
        "A girl who fell down a rabbit hole into Wonderland, and stepped through a mirror. Lewis Carroll, 1865.",
        listOf(
            Joke("Curiouser and curiouser! A man who pushes a rock up a hill.", "In Wonderland, that would be quite normal."),
            Joke("The Hatter asked me: why is a raven like a writing-desk?", "He had no answer. Do you? No? Then push on."),
            Joke("The White Queen believed six impossible things before breakfast.", "A rock that you push forever is only one. You are doing well."),
            Joke("I fell down a rabbit hole for a very long time.", "Then I had to climb out. I know how you feel."),
            Joke("Riddle: what gets bigger the more you take away from it?", "A hole. Mine was a rabbit hole."),
            Joke("The Cheshire Cat told me that we are all mad.", "He meant you too, I think. In the nicest way."),
            Joke("In the race of the Dodo, everybody won, and all had prizes.", "Your prize is the top. Then the race starts again."),
            Joke("Riddle: what has a mouth but never eats, and runs but never walks?", "A river. It runs downhill, which is the easy way."),
            Joke("Riddle: a face, two hands, and it lives in a waistcoat pocket.", "The White Rabbit's watch. It only ever told him one thing: late, late, late!"),
            Joke("I shut up like a telescope, till I was only ten inches high.", "Then I could not reach the key on the table. There is always a catch. Yours is round."),
            Joke("I give myself very good advice, though I very seldom follow it.", "My advice to you: rest at the top, and look at the view. You may follow it or not."),
            Joke("Four times five is twelve, and four times six is thirteen, and so on.", "I would never get to twenty at that rate. Please do not count your climbs my way."),
            Joke("Riddle: take a bone from a dog. What remains?", "The dog's temper, said the Red Queen. I think I would not remain either."),
            Joke("The Mouse said: mine is a long and a sad tale!", "It is a long tail, certainly, I said. But why do you call it sad? He did not laugh."),
            Joke("The Lory said: I am older than you, and must know better.", "And it would not tell its age, so there was no more to be said. Rocks are like that."),
            Joke("A little Crab said: Ma, you would try the patience of an oyster!", "I think you have the patience of an oyster. Two oysters. A whole bed of them."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is round, never late, and waits at the bottom?", "Your rock. The White Rabbit could learn a thing or two from it."),
            Joke("When I grew very tall, I said goodbye to my feet. So far away!", "I meant to send them new boots every Christmas, by post. With my love."),
            Joke("I pretend to be two people. Once I cheated myself at croquet.", "So I boxed my own ears. If you were two people, one could push while one rests."),
            Joke("London is the capital of Paris, and Paris is the capital of Rome.", "My geography went wrong in Wonderland. Is the top the capital of the hill?"),
            Joke("Riddle: what is left of a cat, when the cat goes away tail first?", "The grin. The Cheshire Cat's grin stayed for some time after the rest of him had gone."),
            Joke("In the looking-glass, your rock would roll uphill by itself.", "And you would run after it, backwards. What a sight! Shall I find you a big mirror?"),
            Joke("The Mouse told us the driest thing he knew, to dry us off.", "It was all about William the Conqueror. We stayed just as wet. History is not a towel."),
            Joke("The White Rabbit took me for his maid, and sent me home for his gloves.", "How queer, to run errands for a rabbit! Next, Dinah will send me. Who sends you?"),
            Joke("Riddle: divide a loaf by a knife. What is the answer?", "Bread-and-butter, of course. The Red Queen said it before I could."),
            Joke("A very big puppy came to play with me. Or else I was very small.", "I threw it a stick, and it ran after it. You would like a dog that fetches rocks."),
            Joke("Do cats eat bats? Do bats eat cats? I could not answer either one.", "So it did not matter which way I put it. Up the hill, or down: it is the same hill."),
            Joke("In the Rabbit's house I grew so big that one foot went up the chimney.", "Out flew Bill the Lizard, like a sky-rocket. Your rock goes the other way, I see."),
            Joke("Riddle: who may look at a king, and need not bow?", "A cat. I read that in some book. The Cheshire Cat looked, and grinned."),
            Joke("The Caterpillar asked me: who are you?", "I hardly knew. I had changed so often since morning. You know who you are. Lucky."),
            Joke("The Pigeon took me for a serpent, because my neck was so very long.", "Little girls eat eggs too, I said. Then they are a kind of serpent, said the Pigeon."),
            Joke("The Duchess's Footman said he would sit by the door till tomorrow.", "On and off, for days and days, he said. You go up and down for days and days. Better."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is one and one and one and one and one and one?", "I lost count when the White Queen asked me. Like your pushes. Nobody could count those."),
            Joke("I used to think fairy tales never happened. Then I was in one!", "There ought to be a book written about me. And one about you, with a rock in it."),
            Joke("Pebbles came flying at me, and turned into little cakes.", "If your rock ever turns into a cake, only eat a bit. Cakes change you."),
            Joke("Which way? I asked the Cheshire Cat. Where to? he asked back.", "You want the top. So it is up. You are sure to get there, if you only walk long enough."),
            Joke("Riddle: what climbs all day, and never grows any taller?", "You. I climbed nothing, and grew nine feet tall. Wonderland is not fair at all."),
            Joke("The Hare buttered the Hatter's watch. It was the best butter.", "But crumbs got in, and the watch went two days wrong. Never butter your rock."),
            Joke("The Mock Turtle sat sad and lonely on a little ledge of rock.", "He sobbed. It is all his fancy, said the Gryphon. You have a real rock, and you smile."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is the cause of lightning?", "The thunder, I said. No, the other way round! Too late, said the Red Queen."),
            Joke("It is no use going back to yesterday. I was a different girl then.", "Not you, I think. Yesterday you were just what you are today: brave, and pushing."),
            Joke("Mind the sense, said the Duchess, and sounds will mind themselves.", "So mind the push, and the top will mind itself. That is my moral for you."),
            Joke("Three inches high is a very good height, said the Caterpillar.", "It was exactly three inches high, so I did not argue. Your rock is a good size too."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is the oldest rule in the King of Hearts' book?", "Rule Forty-two, he said. Then it ought to be Number One, I said. He shut the book."),
            Joke("The Queen played croquet with flamingoes and hedgehogs.", "My hedgehog unrolled and walked off. Your rock only rolls downhill. Much more polite."),
            Joke("Dormouse logic: I breathe when I sleep, so I sleep when I breathe.", "True, for him. And for you: I push when I climb, and I climb when I push."),
            Joke("The Mock Turtle studied Reeling, Writhing and Uglification.", "And Drawling, and Fainting in Coils. I only learned French and music."),
            Joke("Riddle: when is a hill a valley?", "When the Red Queen is near. She has seen hills that would make yours a valley."),
            Joke("If I had your rock, I would give it a name. Dinah, perhaps.", "No, Dinah is my cat. She would not like that. Let us call it Mabel. Hello, Mabel!"),
            Joke("The White Knight fell off his horse every few steps.", "Plenty of practice! he said. You have plenty too. And you never fall off your rock."),
            Joke("The Gryphon said: explanations take such a dreadful time.", "So I never asked why you push the rock. Push first. Explain some other day."),
            Joke("Riddle: what are tarts made of?", "Pepper, mostly, said the Cook. Treacle, said a sleepy voice: the Dormouse."),
            Joke("The Queen of Hearts shouts: off with his head! all day long.", "It is all her fancy, said the Gryphon. They never executes nobody. Not even once."),
            Joke("The Hatter sang, and the Queen cried: he is murdering the time!", "Since then, Time will not do a thing he asks. Be kind to Time. You spend a lot together."),
            Joke("The Mock Turtle had ten hours of lessons, then nine, then eight.", "So the eleventh day was a holiday. And the twelfth? Enough lessons, said the Gryphon."),
            Joke("Riddle: what can you see on an empty road, with very good eyes?", "Nobody. The White King wished he had my eyes, to see Nobody so far off."),
            Joke("Let us pretend the glass is soft, like gauze, I told my kitten.", "And it was! I went right through. Pretending works. Pretend your rock is a bun."),
            Joke("A Looking-glass book had all its words the wrong way round.", "I held it to a mirror: Jabberwocky. Somebody killed something: that is clear."),
            Joke("The jury wrote their names down, so as not to forget them.", "Before the end of the trial! Perhaps write yours on your rock. Just in case."),
            Joke("Riddle: which side of the mushroom makes you grow taller?", "The left. The right made my chin bump my foot. I had to try both to find out."),
            Joke("The Queen of Hearts should make a rule: rocks stay at the top.", "Rule Forty-three. Your rock would not listen. Rocks never read the rules."),
            Joke("At the Mad Tea-Party, they move round as the cups get used up.", "What happens when you come to the beginning again? I asked. They changed the subject."),
            Joke("The White King said: the horror! I shall never, never forget it!", "You will, though, said the Queen, if you do not make a memorandum of it."),
            Joke("Riddle: why is a whiting called a whiting?", "It does the boots and shoes under the sea, said the Gryphon. Soles and eels, of course."),
            Joke("I walked to a hill, but the path kept taking me back to the house.", "A flower told me to walk the other way. It worked! Do not try it with a rock."),
            Joke("Behind the glass, the clock had an old man's face, and grinned.", "Clocks should not grin. That is a job for cats. Cheshire ones."),
            Joke("Riddle: jaws that bite, claws that catch, and eyes of flame.", "The Jabberwock. Do not worry. It lives in a poem, and poems stay where they are."),
            Joke("Off with her head! cried the Queen at me. Nobody moved.", "Who cares for you? I said. You are nothing but a pack of cards! And then I woke up."),
            Joke("As I left, they were putting the Dormouse into the teapot.", "He did not even wake. Some can sleep through anything. You can push through anything."),
            Joke("The Hatter could not stand down. He was on the floor already.", "Then you may sit down, said the King. Some days, that is the best advice of all."),
            Joke("Riddle: why did the Mock Turtle call his old teacher Tortoise?", "Because he taught us, said the Mock Turtle. He thought me very dull for asking."),
            Joke("If I nibbled the left side of the mushroom, I would be as tall as a tree.", "Then your rock would be a pebble to me. I could pop it on the top for you. Just once."),
            Joke("In Looking-glass chess, a pawn who reaches the end is a queen.", "You walk to the top every day. You ought to be a king by now. A bishop, at least."),
            Joke("The Tiger-lily talks, when anybody is worth talking to.", "Then all the flowers talked at once. So I was worth talking to. So are you."),
            Joke("Riddle: what lives on weak tea with cream in it?", "The Bread-and-butter-fly. Its head is a lump of sugar."),
            Joke("On the Looking-glass train, a word costs a thousand pounds.", "So I said nothing at all. Your rock never says a word. It must be very rich."),
            Joke("I ran with the Red Queen, and we stayed under the same tree.", "All the running you can do keeps you in the same place, she said. You two would get on."),
            Joke("In the Lobster Quadrille, you throw the lobsters far out to sea.", "Then you swim after them. Like you and your rock, after it rolls. Only wetter."),
            Joke("Riddle: what time is it at the Hatter's table, all day long?", "Six o'clock. Always tea-time, so there is never time to wash the cups."),
            Joke("The White King has two Messengers: one to come, and one to go.", "I beg your pardon? I said. It is not respectable to beg, said the King."),
            Joke("I grew in court. The Dormouse said: you have no right to grow!", "I cannot help it, I said, I am growing. You cannot help pushing. It is the same."),
            Joke("In Jabberwocky, the father cries: O frabjous day! Callooh! Callay!", "He chortled in his joy, the poem says. Try it at the top. Chortling is good for you."),
            Joke("Riddle: it came yesterday, and it comes tomorrow, but never today.", "Jam, at the White Queen's. Jam every other day, and today is never any other day."),
            Joke("In the wood where things have no names, I forgot my own.", "I knew it began with L. It does not, of course. Yours begins with S, in case you forget."),
            Joke("The White Knight trains his hair up a stick, like a fruit-tree.", "Things never fall upwards, you know, he said. Your rock agrees with him."),
            Joke("The Hatter told me my hair wanted cutting.", "No personal remarks, I said. It is very rude. Your rock looks very nice today."),
            Joke("Riddle: what does no wise fish go anywhere without?", "A porpoise. Off on a journey? With what porpoise? the Mock Turtle would ask."),
            Joke("Tweedledee said: you won't make yourself a bit realler by crying.", "So I stopped. You never cry over your rock, I see. You must be very real indeed."),
            Joke("When I came to the Eighth Square, I found a crown on my head.", "Queen Alice! Then two Queens fell asleep on my shoulders. Being a queen is hard work."),
            Joke("A Rocking-horse-fly is wooden, and swings from tree to tree.", "It lives on sap and sawdust. If your rock had wings, would it be a Rock-fly?"),
            Joke("Riddle: when may you wear a hat that is not yours?", "When you are a hatter. The Hatter keeps his to sell. He has none of his own."),
            Joke("A voice on the train said I should be labelled: Lass, with care.", "Like glass, with care. I would label your rock: Rock, with care. This way up."),
            Joke("Running with the Red Queen, I asked her: are we nearly there?", "Nearly there! she cried. We passed it ten minutes ago! Faster! I never even saw it."),
            Joke("The White King eats hay when faint. Nothing like it, he says.", "Not that nothing is better, mind. Just nothing like it. Hay at the top, perhaps?"),
            Joke("Riddle: what can you take more of, when you have had none?", "Tea. It is very easy to take more than nothing, said the Hatter."),
            Joke("In the wood with no names, a Fawn walked by my side.", "At the edge it knew I was a girl, and ran away. Names spoil things, a little."),
            Joke("Tweedledum and Tweedledee meant to fight over a rattle.", "They put on bolsters and a saucepan helmet. Then a crow came, and both ran off."),
            Joke("Riddle: why carry a box upside down?", "So the rain cannot get in, said the White Knight. The lid was open. Out fell everything."),
            Joke("The White Queen screams first, and pricks her finger after.", "She has done all the screaming already, she says. Why do it twice? Very sensible."),
            Joke("The Red Queen said: curtsey while you think. It saves time.", "So I curtsey to your rock while I think what to say. It looks very pleased."),
            Joke("The King said: begin at the beginning, go to the end, then stop.", "You do the first two very well. The stopping, never. I think that is braver."),
            Joke("Riddle: what did three little sisters draw, down in the well?", "All things that begin with M: mouse-traps, the moon, memory and muchness."),
            Joke("To gyre, said Humpty Dumpty, is to go round like a gyroscope.", "Your rock gyres all the way down. It does not gimble, I hope. That is making holes."),
            Joke("Tweedledee said: if it were so, it would be.", "But as it isn't, it ain't. That's logic. Your rock rolls down. That is logic too."),
            Joke("The White Knight carries a beehive. No bee has come near it yet.", "He is still very hopeful. I like hopeful people. You are one too."),
            Joke("Riddle: the more I walked toward it, the further off it got.", "The egg in the Sheep's shop. When at last I got to it, it was Humpty Dumpty."),
            Joke("The White Queen lives backwards. Her memory works both ways.", "She remembers best what happens the week after next. She says your rock goes up."),
            Joke("The Red Queen said: even a joke should have some meaning.", "So mine all have one. This one means: I think you are very brave."),
            Joke("The Queen of Hearts said: sentence first, verdict afterwards.", "Stuff and nonsense! I said. It is a good thing to say. Try it when the rock rolls down."),
            Joke("Riddle: like a badger, a lizard and a corkscrew. What is it?", "A tove. Humpty Dumpty says they nest under sundials, and live on cheese."),
            Joke("The Unicorn thought I was a fabulous monster. I thought he was.", "So we made a bargain: if you believe in me, I will believe in you. I believe in you!"),
            Joke("The White Knight would climb a gate by standing on his head on it.", "Then the feet are high enough, he said. He had not tried it yet. It might be hard."),
            Joke("The prettiest rushes were always just out of my reach.", "Like the top, some days, I should think. But the ones I picked were lovely too."),
            Joke("The White Queen said: consider how far you have come today.", "Consider anything, only do not cry! So I consider your rock. It is very round."),
            Joke("The Red Queen told me: speak only when you are spoken to.", "Then nobody would ever say anything, I said. So I spoke first. Hello!"),
            Joke("Was it my dream or the Red King's? I was in his, and he in mine.", "Which do you think? If someone dreams you and your rock, I hope it is a kind dream."),
            Joke("A wabe, said Humpty Dumpty, goes a long way before and behind.", "So your path is a wabe: a long way before you, and a long way behind."),
            Joke("Riddle: the Lion and the Unicorn fight for a crown. Whose crown is it?", "The White King's. The best of the joke, he said, is that it is mine all the while."),
            Joke("I asked the White Knight if his song was very long.", "It is long, he said, but very, very beautiful. Your climb is like that, I think."),
            Joke("Riddle: fivepence farthing for one, but twopence for two. What is it?", "An egg, in the Sheep's shop. But if you buy two, you must eat them both."),
            Joke("The White Queen said: nobody can do two things at once.", "She cannot, and I cannot. You push a rock and smile at me at once. Very clever."),
            Joke("The Red Queen said: Alice, Mutton. Mutton, Alice. And the mutton bowed.", "It is not polite to cut anyone you have been introduced to, she said. So, no dinner."),
            Joke("Riddle: which cake do you hand round first, and cut afterwards?", "A Looking-glass cake. It came apart by itself as I carried it round."),
            Joke("The White Knight said: over that brook, and you will be a queen.", "I waved my handkerchief till he was out of sight. Now I wave it at you."),
        ),
    ),
    Joker(
        2, "Red Riding Hood", 62,
        "A girl who met a wolf on the way to her grandmother, in the tale of Charles Perrault, 1697.",
        listOf(
            Joke("Is this the way to my grandmother's house?", "Past the man with the rock? Oh, that is you. Thank you!"),
            Joke("Grandmother, what big ears you have!", "That was the wolf. Now I look at the ears first."),
            Joke("What do wolves say when they meet?", "Howl do you do?"),
            Joke("I have cake and wine for my grandmother.", "Here, have a crumb. Pushing is hungry work."),
            Joke("My mother said: do not leave the path.", "You never leave the path. She would like you."),
            Joke("Riddle: what is red, has a basket, and is never late?", "Me. Well, once. There was a wolf."),
            Joke("My red cap is of velvet. I never wear anything else.", "And you never push anything else. We both know what suits us."),
            Joke("A red hood in France, a red cap in Germany.", "Either way, the wolves see me coming. Red is not a color for hiding."),
            Joke("Mother said: walk nicely, and mind the bottle.", "You walk very nicely. And lucky you: a rock does not break. It only rolls."),
            Joke("Mother said: say good morning before you peep.", "Good morning! There. Now may I peep at your rock? Oh, what a fine one."),
            Joke("Grandmother lives under three big oak trees.", "Come for tea one day. Knock twice and say your name. We have had wolves."),
            Joke("A wolf said: You walk as if you were going to school!", "You walk like that too. But you have a good reason. It is a very big rock."),
            Joke("I saw a flower, then a prettier one, farther on.", "Like your top: always a little farther on. But you get there. I got lost."),
            Joke("On the long way, I ran after butterflies.", "You never chase butterflies. Your hands are full. I will chase one for you."),
            Joke("The wolf said: Let us race to Grandmother's!", "He took the short way. You have no short way. But no wolf races you, either."),
            Joke("Grandmother says: Pull the bobbin, and the latch goes up.", "If only rocks were like that. Pull the bobbin, and up goes the rock!"),
            Joke("Grandmother's door had a latch. Then the wolf came.", "Now it has a latch, a bolt, two locks, and a very loud goose."),
            Joke("A wolf knocked and said: Open! I am Red Riding Hood!", "But I was inside, with Grandmother. We just kept eating our cake."),
            Joke("The wolf sat on the roof and smelled sausages.", "He leaned and leaned, and slid into the trough. Splash! Silly grey-beard."),
            Joke("I sing all the way through the wood.", "Mother says it keeps the wolves away. The birds too. I am not a good singer."),
            Joke("The huntsman heard loud snores at Grandmother's.", "It was the wolf, in her cap. Grandmother never snores. Well, only a little."),
            Joke("Grandmother ate the cake and drank the wine.", "She was well at once. Cake and wine fix most things. Not rocks, though."),
            Joke("A wolf said good morning, with a wicked look.", "I said good morning back, and walked on. Manners are free. So are legs."),
            Joke("The wolf went round and round Grandmother's house.", "He never gave up. Like you! But you have much better manners."),
            Joke("Mother sent Grandmother a cake and a little pot of butter.", "Butter on your rock? It might slide up easier. Or down. Better not."),
            Joke("Wolves try no tricks when woodcutters are near.", "So I like strong folk about. You will do. You and your big rock."),
            Joke("Is that a rock, or a wolf curled up very small?", "A rock. Good. A wolf would never let you push him like that."),
            Joke("Why do wolves never push rocks?", "Too much work. A wolf would rather lie in bed, in a nightcap, and wait."),
            Joke("How do you tell a wolf from a grandmother?", "Ask her to knit. Wolves drop every stitch."),
            Joke("A wolf once told me how sweetly the birds sing in the wood.", "He was right about that. Wrong about everything else."),
            Joke("The wolf said: Big hands are the better to hug you with.", "Your hands are big too. Give your rock a hug from me."),
            Joke("The wolf had big eyes, the better to see me with.", "Yet he never saw the huntsman come in. So much for big eyes."),
            Joke("Grandmother, what a deep voice you have!", "I thought she had a cold. It was worse. It was a wolf."),
            Joke("A wolf asked me the way to Grandmother's house.", "I sent him the long way: up a hill, behind a man with a rock. Sorry!"),
            Joke("Oh, what a big rock you have!", "And you did not say: The better to eat you with! Good. You are not a wolf."),
            Joke("Grandmother says: the sweetest wolves are the worst.", "So if someone is too sweet, I look for a tail. No tail on you. Good."),
            Joke("Let me put a flower on your rock.", "There! A happy rock. It may roll down, but it will roll down pretty."),
            Joke("I wonder what your rock would say, if it could talk.", "Wheee! That is my guess. Rocks must love the way down."),
            Joke("Grandmother's house is the first one past the mill.", "If your rock rolls that far, she will send it back. With a cake for you."),
            Joke("Monsieur Perrault ended my tale with the wolf.", "The Brothers Grimm sent a huntsman. I like their ending much better."),
            Joke("Never call a wolf in a nightcap Grandmother.", "Say: Good morning, wolf! Then run. Downhill is fastest. Ask your rock."),
            Joke("I counted the wolves in the wood. None!", "That is the best number of wolves. Next best: one, far away, fast asleep."),
            Joke("Wolves walk on four legs, and you push with two arms.", "Who is faster? The wolf. Who is stronger? You. Who is nicer? Not the wolf."),
            Joke("I am not afraid of the wood. Of wolves, a little.", "And of rocks that roll down hills. Please hold on tight."),
            Joke("What do you call a wolf who stays on the path?", "Lost. Wolves never stay on the path. That is how you can tell."),
            Joke("My basket goes to Grandmother. Your rock goes up.", "We both do our rounds. But mine ends with cake."),
            Joke("A rock by the door keeps wolves away, they say.", "May I borrow yours? Oh. You are using it. Forever? Never mind, then."),
            Joke("The Brothers Grimm say I went home joyously.", "Joyously! What a word. Try it on your rock. Push joyously!"),
            Joke("Riddle: thirty white horses on a red hill.", "Teeth! The wolf had a whole herd. Grandmother has six, and she loves each one."),
